Use the lock-selected psycopg 3 (binary extra) for PostgreSQL access and the lock-selected keyring for credential lookup, calling their real APIs directly.
BasedPyright narrowing: iterate CottList values directly; narrow Option with isinstance(value, Some) and treat the else branch as Nothing; narrow the last remaining union variant without another isinstance test.
psycopg typing: build libpq conninfo with psycopg.conninfo.make_conninfo and pass it positionally to psycopg.connect together with explicit keyword options such as autocommit and connect_timeout; never expand a dict[str, str] into the overloaded keyword parameters of psycopg.connect. psycopg.conninfo.conninfo_to_dict returns values typed str | int | None: narrow each one explicitly instead of annotating the mapping as dict[str, str | None].
psycopg typing: pass user-authored SQL text to Cursor.execute encoded as UTF-8 bytes; keep fixed SQL as LiteralString literals and compose identifiers with psycopg.sql.Identifier. psycopg.Error.diag is not optional. isinstance(value, memoryview) yields memoryview[Unknown]; cast(memoryview[int], value) before bytes(value).
JSON typing: json.loads returns Any; after an isinstance list or dict test cast to list[object] or dict[object, object] before iterating, indexing or len, and check every element before use.
subprocess typing: annotate text-mode processes as subprocess.Popen[str] and subprocess.CompletedProcess[str], and binary ones with [bytes]; an unparameterized Popen makes its streams Unknown.
Error helpers return the declared error union type (for example Err[<ErrorEnum>]), not a variant-specific Err, so they compose with the function's Result type. Path values are pathlib.Path: pass them to os.fspath or open directly, without isinstance(os.PathLike) tests.
cott-domain real.pgcli.run return: annotate the return type as typing.Never exactly, not typing.NoReturn.
cott-domain real.pgcli.resolve_credential return: getpass.getpass warns with getpass.GetPassWarning before falling back to echoed input; call it inside warnings.catch_warnings() with warnings.simplefilter("error", getpass.GetPassWarning) so that fallback raises instead.
cott-domain real.pgcli.page_output return: BasedPyright types the stdin stream of a subprocess.Popen[str] as IO[Any] or IO[str], which is not assignable to typing.TextIO; annotate stream helper parameters as typing.IO[str].
cott-domain real.pgcli.import_delimited return: BasedPyright reports reportUnnecessaryIsInstance for an isinstance test that cannot fail; do not test isinstance(value, bytes | bytearray) on a value already typed bytes, such as the result of cott_runtime._cott_fixture_read or a binary file read.
